From: Paul Wouters <paul@xtdnet.nl>
To: Brian Macy <bmacy@sunshinecomputing.com>
Cc: axp-list@redhat.com <axp-list@redhat.com>
Date: Tuesday, February 03, 1998 9:17 AM
Subject: Re: MILO soft reboot problems...

>> I've noticed a new problem with MILO on soft reboots. When I get the
prompt
>> Press any key to continue or Esc to boot (something like that) it
>> immediately drops to a MILO> prompt and is followed by a bunch of " O>"
>> strings and the computer locks up. If I hard boot the machine than it
works
>> perfectly fine. I tried re-dd'ing the MILO partition with a fresh RedHat
5.0
>> MILO noname image but that didn't change anything. I also noticed last
night
>> that I got some nasty NVRAM has problems message on boot-up.
>
>This is quite normal actually :)
>You have a MILO image that has serial console support. When soft rebooting,
>MILO sends output to the serial console. You likely have a modem connected
and
>on, and it will be confused by all the messages MILO is telling it. So it
says
>"ERROR". MILO happily responds to that, and you end up with a line of input
that
>reaches the max, and transmission will stop (MILO will then only allow you
do
>use backspace to delete input scharacters.
>Turn of your modem during reboot, or recompile milo without serial console
>support.
>
>Paul
>

