From: Toon Moene <toon@moene.indiv.nluug.nl>
Subject: Re: f2c Errors

>  We seem to be having a problem with f2c (RedHat 4.2).
>
>  At the end of almost every sub-routine, we get a floating
>  point exception (during the f2c run).
>
>  This works VERY well under Intel Linux (RedHat 4.2).

Yes, it's a coding error in f2c that has been fixed long ago - it  
might well be that Red Hat has a new f2c rpm on their site ...

>  We've tried g77, and the egcs g77, and both work well...
>  except that we need double precision, and they don't
>  support that, while f2c does.

What you probably mean is that g77 doesn't support a command line  
option to treat REAL variables, arrays and constants as 8-byte  
quantities.  Indeed, it doesn't (how about funding this change ?).  
OTOH, g77 - like any Fortran 77 conformant compiler - *has* to  
support the type DOUBLE PRECISION.

HTH,
Toon.

