From przemek@rrdjazz.nist.gov Tue Feb 24 14:58:40 1998
Message-ID: <199802231437.JAA04904@rrdjazz.nist.gov>
Date: Mon, 23 Feb 1998 09:37:14 -0500
From: Przemek Klosowski <przemek@rrdjazz.nist.gov>
Subject: Re: gcc compiler warning

I've got a program which gets the following warnings when I compile with
   -Wall.  Can anyone tell me what this is trying to say?  How would these
   varibles get "clobbered"?  How can I prevent this?

   function `gpi_EvaluateGeneration':
   gpi.c:336: warning: variable `i' might    be clobbered by `longjmp' or `vfork'

Register-based local variables are not guaranteed to be preserved
across longjump (and also I guess vfork); in other words if you do
setjmp, and then longjmp to it, you aren't guaranteed to see the
values of register-based local variables as they were at time of
setjmp; this is because setjmp/longjmp save/restore the stack only.

