Hi,

I'm using IPX on my Alpha since 2.0.32 w/o problems, the
attached patches applied.

On 24/2/98 0:00:39 you wrote:
>
>Sorry about any ambiguity but this message is referring to IPX the
protocall not IPX the sun box :)
>
>On Mon, 23 Feb 1998 mike@alpha.lab.realminfo.com wrote:
>
>>
>> Any reason why this shouldent work? I noticed that all the IPX stuff is
>> for either sparc or i386 arch's...compiled mars and it compiled fine. So
> why dosent IPX work?
>>

IPX doesn't work, because on 2.0.x the IPX network number is
defined as long, which works for 32 bit architectures only.

(See attached file: linux2.0.32-alpha-ipx-diffs.gz)(See attached file:
ipxripd-0.7-alpha-diff2.gz)(See attached file: ncpfs-2.0.11-alpha-diffs.gz)

The patches fix this (use 'int' for IPX network number).

Really needed only is the linux2.0.32-alpha-ipx-patch, the
others are for ipxd and ncpfs, if you use them.
(Find ipxripd and ncpfs tools on
ftp://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/linux/misc/ncpfs )

The kernel patch is for 2.0.32, but should apply cleanly to
2.0.33, too. (I'm running it here on 2.0.33 and cannot
remember problems applying the patch....)

I never tried mars on an alpha, but maybe you will have to
look at the definition of the IPX network number and fix
it there too....

regards,
chris

