Subject: Re: jdk-1.1.5-2
In-Reply-To: <Pine.LNX.3.96.980222222716.1123G-100000@octavia.wopr>

On Sun, 22 Feb 1998, Joakim Roubert wrote:

> On Sun, 22 Feb 1998, Hugo van der Kooij wrote:
> 
> > > octavia:~# rpm -ba /usr/src/redhat/SPECS/jdk-1.1.5.spec  
> > > Package lookup failed: -p /sbin/ldconfig
> > > Build failed.
> > > octavia:~# 
> 
> > > %post -p /sbin/ldconfig
> > > %postun -p /sbin/ldconfig
> > > 
> > > What is this supposed to do?
> > Initiate the libraries. If you have a normal (redhat) system this file
> > MUST be present.
> 
> Ah. I thought it might be something that important, yes....
> 
> > Make sure you have the dynamic library stuff or suffer with things like
> > this.
> 
> How do I make sure...? I have a normal RH 4.1 with some upgrades. It
> should be very normal...
> 
> I got the SRPM from a redhat-mirror.

You need to get it from the CD again.

Here is a bit from the manpage:

       ldconfig creates the necessary links and cache (for use by
       the run-time linker, ld.so)  to  the  most  recent  shared
       libraries  found  in the directories specified on the com-
       mand line, in the file /etc/ld.so.conf, and in the trusted
       directories  (/usr/lib  and  /lib).   ldconfig  checks the
       header and file names of  the  DLL's  it  encounters  when
       determining   which   versions  should  have  their  links
       updated.  

I am not absolute sure in which package it is with RHL 4.1 but it is in
ldconfig-1.9.5-2 here on RHL 5.0

I suggest you find it and install it immediate.

Hugo.

