Subject: Re: axppci33 problems with mouse SOLVED! - typos

Others have pointed out that this pinout is not unique to Digital.
   Whether or not Digital invented it, will remain unknown until
   someone can come up with an x86 board that predates the noname
   and shares the pinout. I admit, it does seem easier to make a
   ribbon cable mate to DB9 in this fashion. The split and overlap
   form is more of a pain to handle.

Not to extend the discussion beyond a polite duration, but as I said,
there are certainly PC MBs in both styles, dating pretty far back.

Split/overlap cabling is I guess easier to solder (you don't have to spread
up and down the ribbon), but is impossible to do for larger connectors
like the parallel port, so it leads to an inconsistent cabling scheme
(up/down for parallel, split/overlap for serial).

